WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.886
Not every serious OT event begins with an external attacker.

00:00:04.886 --> 00:00:14.021
Configuration mistakes, weak change control, excessive privileges, and ordinary operational errors can disrupt production or create pathways for later compromise.

00:00:14.021 --> 00:00:18.908
These risks deserve the same disciplined analysis as malicious threats.

00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:25.494
An incorrect firewall rule may expose a control network or block a required communication.

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:32.929
A change to controller logic or an HMI screen may affect process behavior or operator decisions.

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:38.665
Engineering workstations are especially sensitive because their tools can modify many devices.

00:00:38.665 --> 00:00:45.676
Using them for email, web browsing, or unrelated administration expands both error and malware exposure.

00:00:45.676 --> 00:00:50.562
Poor change control makes failures harder to detect and reverse.

00:00:50.562 --> 00:01:00.547
Teams should know what changed, who approved it, what was tested, when it was deployed, and how to restore the previous state.

00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:06.708
Emergency changes may be necessary, but they still require follow-up documentation and review.

00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:12.019
Excessive privilege increases the consequence of a mistake or compromised account.

00:01:12.019 --> 00:01:16.056
Separate routine operation, engineering, administration, and vendor roles.

00:01:16.056 --> 00:01:24.766
Use individual identities where systems support them, control shared emergency credentials, and review access when personnel or contracts change.

00:01:24.766 --> 00:01:30.502
Insider risk includes malicious action, but prevention cannot rely on distrust alone.

00:01:30.502 --> 00:01:40.062
Clear procedures, usable tools, peer review for sensitive changes, training, monitoring, and a healthy reporting culture reduce accidental and intentional misuse.

00:01:40.062 --> 00:01:48.772
Operators should be able to report unexpected behavior without fear that every anomaly will be treated as personal failure.

00:01:48.772 --> 00:01:53.234
Human reliability improves when the system supports good decisions.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:02:01.519
Maintain accurate diagrams and backups, make approved access easier than workarounds, test changes, and learn from near misses.

00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:09.805
OT security is partly the engineering of conditions in which one mistake does not become a facility-wide incident.
